<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH-FLOOD-BONDS.</title>
<headline>CZECH-FLOOD-BONDS.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech Prime Minister Vaclav Klaus said on Tuesday he expected bonds aimed at raising funds for flood relief programmes to be launched on August 1.</p>
<p>He said the bonds will have a maturity of five years and a net yield that &quot;roughly covers&quot; inflation.</p>
<p>&quot;Our intention is to find a value, which would mean that net yield, after taxation, roughly covers inflation,&quot; he said, adding that the coupon would not be fixed.</p>
</text>
